    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 1967 when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> took power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> as British rule in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> ended.</li><li>The only Marxist–Leninist state in the Arab world, ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemeni-socialist-party">Yemeni Socialist Party</a> and allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>.</li><li>A party civil war in 1986 and the end of Soviet support led to unification with North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> on 22 May 1990.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>South Yemen’s Family Law of 1974 restricted polygamy and set a minimum age of marriage, making it one of the most progressive family codes in the Arab world.</p></aside>
    </section>

